# Mirror only each account's INBOX into ~/Mail. The [Unified] aerc account
# (notmuch) reads this tree and exposes combined virtual folders; everything
# else (archives, sent, trash) stays on the servers and is read through the
# individual IMAP accounts, so the local store is bounded by your inboxes.
#
# Archiving or deleting on the server drops the local copy on the next run
# (Expunge Both). Both the login name and the password are read from
# 1Password at run time through ~/.config/aerc/get-cred.nu (cached in the
# login keyring), so no addresses live in this file.

IMAPAccount personal
Host imap.migadu.com
UserCmd "nu --no-config-file ~/.config/aerc/get-cred.nu op://Private/Migadu/username"
PassCmd "nu --no-config-file ~/.config/aerc/get-cred.nu op://Private/Migadu/main-mailbox-password"
TLSType IMAPS

IMAPStore personal-remote
Account personal

MaildirStore personal-local
Path /home/ulsippoi/Mail/Personal/
Inbox /home/ulsippoi/Mail/Personal/INBOX
SubFolders Verbatim

Channel personal
Far :personal-remote:
Near :personal-local:
Patterns "INBOX"
Create Both
Expunge Both
SyncState *

IMAPAccount gmail
Host imap.gmail.com
UserCmd "nu --no-config-file ~/.config/aerc/get-cred.nu op://Private/dtulitrcicexylmwntwjup42qe/username"
PassCmd "nu --no-config-file ~/.config/aerc/get-cred.nu op://Private/dtulitrcicexylmwntwjup42qe/apppassword"
TLSType IMAPS

IMAPStore gmail-remote
Account gmail

MaildirStore gmail-local
Path /home/ulsippoi/Mail/Gmail/
Inbox /home/ulsippoi/Mail/Gmail/INBOX
SubFolders Verbatim

Channel gmail
Far :gmail-remote:
Near :gmail-local:
Patterns "INBOX"
Create Both
Expunge Both
SyncState *
